-- title:
--   r-oldness of the Σ-corner at level Mr
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal{O}$ is a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $p$ is a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, so that $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$ has characteristic $p$. Further, $\bar\rho$ is a [`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22) over $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$, i.e. a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ with $\dim_k V = 2$ which is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; the hypothesis `habs` asserts that the base change of $\bar\rho$ to $\overline{k}$ has no invariant subspace other than $\bot$ and $\top$.
--
--   The level data are: a finite set $S$ of primes with $p \in S$, a non-zero natural number $M$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$ and with $p^{2} \nmid M$, and a finite set $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ containing $p$. The hypotheses on $S_{\min}$ and $M$ are: `hmin`, that for a prime $q \neq p$ one has $q \in S_{\min}$ precisely when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (in the sense that some valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ has an element of its inertia subgroup acting non-trivially); `hMmin`, that every $q \in S_{\min}$ with $q \neq p$ divides $M$; `hMunr`, that a prime $q \neq p$ dividing $M$ but not in $S_{\min}$ satisfies $q^{2} \mid M$; `hM3`, that $q^{2} \mid M$ implies $q^{3} \nmid M$ for primes $q \neq p$; `htame`, that for $q \in S_{\min}$ with $q \neq p$ the representation $\bar\rho$, viewed as a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $k$, has $\mathrm{charpoly} = (X-1)^{2}$ on inertia at every place above $q$; and `hord`, that if $p \mid M$ then $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, i.e. above each place over $p$ there is a free rank-one submodule, spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group and with inertia acting trivially on the quotient.
--
--   The auxiliary prime $r$ is prime with $r \notin S$, $r \nmid M$ and $p \nmid r-1$, and satisfies the no-level-raising condition `hrρ`: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $r$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$, $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^{2} \neq (r+1)^{2}$ in $k$.
--
--   The eigensystem data are: the hypothesis that weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(M)$ have an integral structure, namely that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule spanned by the forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is everything; and a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the $T_{\ell}$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$) to $k$, subject to `hθ`: for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \notin S$, and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring over $\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^{2} - \theta(T_{\ell})X + \ell$.
--
--   The auxiliary level is $L$, non-zero, with $L = Mr$. Here $H1\,N\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$ denotes the group of additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_0(N) \leq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ (written additively) to $\mathcal{O}$, that is $H^{1}(\Gamma_0(N), \mathcal{O})$ with trivial coefficients, and `opFamily` sends the generator $T_{\ell}$ or $U_q$ to the Hecke endomorphism `heckeTL` and $\langle d\rangle$ to `diamondL`.
--
--   At level $L$ the data are: a commutative ring $\mathbb{T}$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$, acting on $H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$ compatibly with the $\mathcal{O}$-action; an `IdempotentSplitting` $Sp$ of $\mathbb{T}$, i.e. complete orthogonal idempotents $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_0,\dots,\mathfrak{m}_{n-1}$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb{T}$ and satisfying $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j \iff i \neq j$; an index $i$ such that the corner submodule $e_i \cdot H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$ is finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$; and functions `tfull`, `cfull` on the generators `Gen L S` (constructors $T_{\ell}$ for $\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$; $U_q$ for $q$ prime dividing $L$; $\langle d \rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/L)^{\times}$) with values in $\mathbb{T}$ and in $\mathcal{O}$. Call a generator $g$ admissible if for every prime $q \mid L$, $g = U_q$ forces $q \mid M$ (so all generators except $U_r$ are admissible). The hypotheses are: `hgen`, that every element of $\mathbb{T}$ acts on $H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$ as some element of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of endomorphisms generated by the `opFamily` images of the admissible generators; `htfull`, that `tfull g` acts as `opFamily g` for admissible $g$; `hcfull`, that $\mathrm{tfull}(g) - \mathrm{cfull}(g) \in \mathfrak{m}_i$ for admissible $g$; and `hcofull`, the converse cofinality statement that any $v$ such that for each admissible $g$ and each $k$ some power $(\mathrm{tfull}(g)-\mathrm{cfull}(g))^{n}$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^{k} \cdot H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$ already lies in the corner submodule. The eigenvalue normalisations are: `hcT`, that the residue of $\mathrm{cfull}(T_{\ell})$ equals $\theta(T_{\ell})$ for primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$; `hcU0`, that $\mathrm{cfull}(U_q) \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ for primes $q \mid L$ with $q \mid M$, $q \neq p$ and $q^{2} \mid M$; `hcUp`, that $\mathrm{cfull}(U_p)$ is a unit when $p \mid L$ and $p \mid M$; and `hcd`, that $\mathrm{cfull}(\langle d\rangle) - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ for all $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/L)^{\times}$. Finally `hocc` asserts that the corner submodule is non-zero and `hfaith` that the corner ring $\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i$ (the corner of $\mathbb{T}$ at the idempotent $e_i$) acts faithfully on it.
--
--   At level $M$ the parallel data are $\mathbb{T}_0$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$ acting compatibly on $H1\,M\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$, an idempotent splitting $Sp_0$ with index $i_0$ whose corner submodule is finite free over $\mathcal{O}$, and functions `tfull₀`, `cfull₀` on `Gen M (insert r S)`, subject to: `hgen₀`, that every element of $\mathbb{T}_0$ acts through the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the whole range of `opFamily` at level $M$ for the set $\{r\} \cup S$; `htfull₀`, that `tfull₀ g` acts as `opFamily g` for every generator; `hcfull₀`, that $\mathrm{tfull}_0(g) - \mathrm{cfull}_0(g) \in \mathfrak{m}_{i_0}$ for every generator; `hcofull₀`, the corresponding cofinality criterion for membership in the corner submodule at level $M$; `hocc₀`, that this corner submodule is non-zero; and `hfaith₀`, faithfulness of $\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ on it.
--
--   The two levels are linked by: `hmatchT`, $\mathrm{cfull}(T_{\ell}) = \mathrm{cfull}_0(T_{\ell})$ for primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$, $\ell \notin \{r\}\cup S$, $\ell \nmid M$; `hmatchU`, $\mathrm{cfull}(U_q) = \mathrm{cfull}_0(U_q)$ for primes $q$ dividing both $L$ and $M$; and `hcd₀`, $\mathrm{cfull}_0(\langle d\rangle) - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$. Moreover $r$ is non-zero and `h1`, `hr'` are the two `LevelLE` data $\mathrm{LevelLE}\,M\,L\,\top\,\top\,1$ and $\mathrm{LevelLE}\,M\,L\,\top\,\top\,r$ (namely $M \mid L$, $1 \mid L/M$ respectively $r \mid L/M$, together with the reduction condition on the subgroups, here trivial), giving the two degeneracy maps $\iota_1, \iota_r : H1\,M\,\top\,\mathcal{O} \to H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$ of `iDegL`, defined by composition with the conjugation homomorphisms $\Gamma_0(L) \to \Gamma_0(M)$. Lastly `hrig` is the rank inequality
--   $$\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}\,e_i \cdot H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O} \le 2\,\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}\,e_{i_0} \cdot H1\,M\,\top\,\mathcal{O}.$$
--
--   The conclusion is a conjunction of four assertions. First, an element $v$ of $H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$ lies in the corner submodule $e_i \cdot H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$ if and only if $v = \iota_1(a) + \iota_r(b)$ for some $a, b$ in the corner submodule $e_{i_0} \cdot H1\,M\,\top\,\mathcal{O}$. Secondly, this representation is unique in the strong sense that $a, b$ in the corner submodule at level $M$ with $\iota_1(a) + \iota_r(b) = 0$ must both vanish. Thirdly, the rank inequality `hrig` is an equality:
--   $$\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}\,e_i \cdot H1\,L\,\top\,\mathcal{O} = 2\,\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}\,e_{i_0} \cdot H1\,M\,\top\,\mathcal{O}.$$
--   Fourthly, there exists an isomorphism $e_R$ of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras from $\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i$ to $\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ such that: $e_R$ carries the image in the corner ring of $\mathrm{tfull}(T_{\ell})$ to the image of $\mathrm{tfull}_0(T_{\ell})$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$, $\ell \notin \{r\}\cup S$ and $\ell \nmid M$; $e_R$ carries the image of $\mathrm{tfull}(U_q)$ to the image of $\mathrm{tfull}_0(U_q)$ for every prime $q$ dividing both $L$ and $M$; and $e_R$ intertwines the actions along the decomposition, in that for every $x \in \mathrm{CornerRing}\,i$, every $a, b$ in the corner submodule at level $M$ and every $v$ in the corner submodule at level $L$ with $v = \iota_1(a) + \iota_r(b)$, one has $x \cdot v = \iota_1(e_R(x)\cdot a) + \iota_r(e_R(x)\cdot b)$.
--
--   This is the transport step to the Taylor–Wiles auxiliary level: at an auxiliary prime $r$ chosen so that $\bar\rho$ admits no level-raising congruence at $r$ and $p \nmid r-1$, the localised cohomology at level $\Gamma_0(Mr)$ is $r$-old, being the direct sum of the two degeneracy images of the localised cohomology at level $\Gamma_0(M)$, with an unchanged corner Hecke algebra. It is used by [`CohCarrier.free_ordinary_sigmaCorner_level_mul`](thm.html#CohCarrier.free_ordinary_sigmaCorner_level_mul), [`CohCarrier.torsionBySet_ne_bot_and_finrank_sigmaCornerSubmodule_auxLevel_eq_mul`](thm.html#CohCarrier.torsionBySet_ne_bot_and_finrank_sigmaCornerSubmodule_auxLevel_eq_mul) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel), which propagate freeness, rank and Hecke-algebra identifications from level $M$ to the auxiliary level.
